    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d977">

                <pb facs="1010" n="996" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg996"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.512337 Shipping/11–2344</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Braden</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4684</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-23">November 23,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department refers to the Embassy’s
                    despatch no. 7879 of September 13, 1944 concerning the exemption from taxation
                    of the revenues obtained in Cuba by vessels owned by or chartered to the War
                    Shipping Administration.</p>
                <p>Now that the new administration has assumed office, the Department is of the
                    opinion that the Embassy should press for a prompt <pb facs="1011" n="997"
                        xml:id="pg997"/> and definite reply to its representations on this subject
                    as originally presented to the Cuban Government in note no. 731 of October 15,
                        1942.<anchor n="49" xml:id="d977-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>G[<hi rendition="#small-caps">reen</hi>] H. H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ackworth</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
